<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>April Storm - 1 - The New Eastern Front, 1996</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;The &lt;STRONG&gt;April Storm &lt;/STRONG&gt;campaign assumes that Boris Yeltsin was removed from power in late&amp;nbsp;1995.&amp;nbsp; His replacement, a former general in the Red Army, has set an aggressive tone for the new Russia.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In the first week of April, 1996,&amp;nbsp;Russia and Belarus invaded parts of eastern Poland.&amp;nbsp; Various reasons, including&amp;nbsp;the large ethnic&amp;nbsp;Ukranian population in this region of Poland, have been offered as justification for the invasion.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Russia has not attempted to move troops further west, but&amp;nbsp;about one quarter of Poland is now under Russian control.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The United Nations has been unable to effect any change.&amp;nbsp; There has&amp;nbsp;been general condemnation of&amp;nbsp;Russia, but its&amp;nbsp;position on the Security Council means it can veto any resolutions that&amp;nbsp;would authorize the use of force against it.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;NATO has warned Russia that the current situation is intolerable and that it must withdraw from Poland or face serious consequences.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
